{"resourceIdentifier":"2610","resourceName":"Unitán afforestation and reforestation of grazing lands project","description":"The project activity “Unitán Afforestation and reforestation of grazing land project” (hereafter, “Unitán project”) is an afforestation project on extensive cattle grazing pastures area and abandoned agricultural lands using native (Schinopsis balansae) and exotic species (various varieties of Eucalyptus including Eucalyptus gxc) aiming to produce, as a priority product, logs for tannin industry and secondarily, fuelwood. The afforestation with this species will prevent the use of timber from native forests in the future.\r\n\r\nUnitán comprises 5 properties located in Chaco and Formosa province, in the NorthEast region of Argentina (the host country), on lightly degraded grassland as a consequence of many decades of extensive cattle grazing and abandoned agriculture land by previous owners. This degradation is expected to continue in the absence of the project. The area of grasslands to be effectively planted and to be included within the Unitán project boundary is then 2,403ha (72.1% of Unitán total area). The unplanted area remaining in part as grassland and native forest remains, become biological corridors used for flora and fauna conservation.\r\n\r\nFrom September 2016 until the time of PDD elaboration, a total area of 939,3 ha of the project was effectively planted. In addition, there is an area of 1,464 ha of planned plantation for the period 2021 to 2025 (mainly in owned and a minor part in leased lands).  In total, the project will have a final scale of about 2,400 ha.\r\n\r\nThe project utilizes two main species: Schinopsis balansae, a native species, and Eucalyptus (different varieties: mainly gxc and cloeziana), occupying 36%, 64% of the total planted area, and with rotation periods of 40 years, 6 and 20, respectively.","location":{"latitude":27.393175,"longitude":59.109475},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod"